{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559","name":"The Imperial Knights","source":{"id":"source:reference-f83f5f82e44c1559","title":"The Imperial Knights","revision":24686,"timestamp":"2024-11-05T18:07:36Z","sha256":"776b29d4d5cdf8b80e8b2dc67279f6cd7988175cbef08751c329ff81e07797e7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24686","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Imperial%20Knights&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f83f5f82e44c1559","blocks":[{"tag":"h4","children":["Description"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Imperial Knights are the personal bodyguards of Emperor ",{"tag":"a","children":["Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Roan_Fel","referenceId":"reference:b68838dc4018d9d2"},". Trained in a variation of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," arts, The Imperial Knights wield ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," as weapons in the defense of their Emperor. Based on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bastion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bastion","referenceId":"reference:863cf03d3363b90e"},", The Imperial Knights are few in number, but are sworn to act to protect the Emperor at all times. Additionally, the Emperor (himself trained as an Imperial Knight) gives the Knights orders and sends them on missions of utmost importance.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Imperial Knights are trained on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Bastion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Bastion","referenceId":"reference:863cf03d3363b90e"}," and learn under a very different training regimen than ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," use. Training of Imperial Knights is usually harsh, but not cruel like ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},". Another difference between ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," and The Imperial Knights is that The Imperial Knights train strictly for combat, not contemplation. The deeper mysterious and philosophies of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," are of little use to The Imperial Knights, who are concerned only with the way ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," can be used as a tool to protect themselves, their comrades, and above all, their Emperor. That is not to say that The Imperial Knights are not aware of or concerned with ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},"; rather, The Imperial Knights teach strict mental discipline and obedience to orders, making them less susceptible to the strong emotions that draw unwary students to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Imperial Knights wear specially crafted armor that uses materials found in the armor of one of the greatest Imperial duelists of all time, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Vader"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Vader","referenceId":"reference:c167be702b56cffc"},". Where Vader's armor was built to intimidate as well as protect, The Imperial Knights wear armor that is purely functional. That, combined with their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cortosis Gauntlets"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cortosis_Gauntlets"},", leaves them constantly prepared for combat no matter where they are. Like most bodyguards, The Imperial Knights are extremely protective, and their vigilance borders on paranoia at times.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Force-Users in the Legacy Era"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Imperial Knights are a small organization that serves ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emperor Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emperor_Roan_Fel"},". Trained in the Jedi arts, The Imperial Knights are far more than mere bodyguards and agents. They are charged with protecting the most wanted individual in the galaxy from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Krayt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Krayt","referenceId":"reference:c6d0b6bc88280f92"},", the self-proclaimed ruler of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},". The Imperial Knights must not only protect their leader physically but also protect his secrecy and keep him from being located by those who would hunt him down. It is the goal of every Imperial Knight to see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Roan_Fel","referenceId":"reference:b68838dc4018d9d2"}," safely returned to his rightful place as Emperor of the galaxy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though The Imperial Knights are trained in many of the same techniques and philosophies as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", their method and credos differ markedly. Where the Jedi Knights spare a good deal of time for contemplation of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," and believe strongly in introspection and meditation, The Imperial Knights take a far more pragmatic view of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". They view ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," as a tool, albeit a powerful one to be respected. They know that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," cannot be used out of anger or selfishness, because even The Imperial Knights know the dangers of falling to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},". The Imperial Knights have little time for any master but the rightful Emperor of the galaxy, and as such there is much less differentiation between Imperial Knights who have trained apprentices and those who have not.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Skilled in the art of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," combat, The Imperial Knights use many of the same combat training techniques as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", and have learned to fight in many of the same ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," dueling styles. However, The Imperial Knights are also the masters of two unique ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," combat forms that place greater emphasis on teamwork than one's individual prowess. The more aggressive style, known as ",{"tag":"i","children":["Praetoria Vonil"]},", focuses on moving quickly and striking hard. The more defensive style, known as ",{"tag":"i","children":["Praetoria Ishu"]},", emphasizes protecting one's allies to allow them to find openings in an opponent's defenses.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Imperial Knight Lightsabers"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["One of the most unique aspects of Imperial Knight training is the manner in which they craft their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},". Though they are heirs to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", they do not follow the Jedi practice of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber Creation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber_Creation"},". Where ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," treat the crafting of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," as a sacred tradition, for The Imperial Knights the creation of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," is given little more significance than learning a new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Power"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Power"}," or fighting style. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," is but a tool, and not a wholly necessary one at that. The Imperial Knights devote as much attention to fighting barehanded, in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", and with ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," as they do to fighting with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Imperial Knights craft ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," using the same methods as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", though with far less ceremony. Additionally, The Imperial Knights do not seek out special crystals from planets like ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ilum"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ilum?action=edit&redlink=1"},", as Jedi did during the days of the Republic. Instead, The Imperial Knights create synthetic crystals using techniques first detailed in Emperor Palpatine's writings, specifically in one of his treatises on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},": ",{"tag":"i","children":["The Book of Anger"]},". Despite the fact that the tome is filled with Dark Side lore, the process of crafting synthetic ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber Crystals"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystals"}," (a method used by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," for millennia to create their red-bladed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},") is little more than a mechanical process, bereft of ceremonial trappings. The Imperial Knights adapted these techniques to create their familiar white-bladed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"},".\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Imperial Knight Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Imperial Knight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_Knight_(CL_10)","referenceId":"reference:1c7e440aa825d547"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Imperial Knight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Imperial_Knight_(CL_11)","referenceId":"reference:4e36481f8777817c"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 11\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Heroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","childr